@doc """
A custom CLI task, invocable as `koja run <name>`.

Packages export tasks in their `koja.toml` by mapping a task name to
the implementing type. Task names are prefixed with the package name,
so a package named `postgres` exports tasks like `postgres.migrate`:

```toml
[tasks]
"postgres.migrate" = "Migrate"
```

The named type implements this protocol. `args` carries everything
after `--` on the command line. Returning `Result.Err` prints the
message to stderr and exits nonzero:

```koja
struct Migrate
end

impl Koja.Task for Migrate
  fn run(args: List<String>) -> Result<(), String>
    IO.puts("running migrations")
    Result.Ok(())
  end
end
```

Tasks exported by a project's dependencies are invocable from that
project too, and `koja tasks` lists every task in scope.
"""
protocol Task
  @doc """
  Executes the task with the command-line arguments after `--`.
  """
  fn run(args: List<String>) -> Result<(), String>
end
